dd24f51b21a9" :answer-field/choices ["q-338004/field-3/668dba9073658905cfbd208ef398f5d3f3cf0216b5f756007174dd24f51b21a9" "q-338004/field-3/0dccd1c0d01f1a6108a63b9727608bbe91e40a553b6f3a4aeaca05919f28c3b7"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-338004" :question/id #uuid "8da06f22-6a38-578e-b590-3e2d4a9025f6" :question/math-academy-id "q-338004" :question/problem "Determine which of the following second-order ODEs are homogeneous, and which are inhomogeneous.$\\,$ The equation $\\,\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{″}-2x{y}^{′}+y=0$ is {{field-1}}. \n\n$\\,$ The equation $\\,{y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}=x$ is {{field-2}}. \n\n$\\,$ The equation $\\,{y}^{″}-xy+4x=0$ is {{field-3}}." :question/worked-solution "Suppose we have a second-order linear ODE given in the form\n\n$$\na(x){y}^{″}+b(x){y}^{′}+c(x)y=f(x).\n$$\n\nThe equation is homogeneous if $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$ If it is not homogeneous, then it is inhomogeneous.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each option.\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{″}-2x{y}^{′}+y=0\n$$\n\nis $\\text{homogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=0$ for all $x.$\n\n- The equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}=x\n$$\n\nis $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=x,$ which is different from zero.\n\n- Writing the equation\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-xy+4x=0\n$$\n\nin the form $a{y}^{″}+b{y}^{′}+cy=f,$ we have\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}-xy=-4x.\n$$\n\nThis equation is $\\text{inhomogeneous}$ since, for the right-hand side, we have $f(x)=-4x,$ which is different from zero." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-338004/field-1" "q-338004/field-2" "q-338004/field-3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "90930e15-0827-5e0b-82cf-98263fc756d6"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-338004"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339254/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "ba04aeca-04dc-5e8f-9ba3-261b61a26a77" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339254/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "8feb8a2a-230c-5cf3-bff7-a3994bb049be" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339254/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "42266fdf-5a26-58dc-89c4-602074a77807" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339254/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "3752d86c-7a3b-5c0e-9a51-0507c31bc467" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339254/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "24d63809-e024-53f3-87cc-61435b10644a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339254/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "11078401-779e-5895-a7c6-38aec08aefe4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-339254/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer-field/choices ["q-339254/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-339254/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-339254/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-339254/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-339254/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339254" :question/id #uuid "d8f4d7ab-4946-517f-88cd-116b43135b3b" :question/math-academy-id "q-339254" :question/problem "Which of the following systems is an initial value problem?\n\n- $x{y}^{″}-4{y}^{′}+4y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x+2x,\\,y(-1)=2,\\,{y}^{′}(2)=0$\n- ${x}^{2}{y}^{″}-{y}^{′}+y=8$\n- $x{y}^{″}+{y}^{′}-3y={e}^{x},\\,y(1)=0,\\,{y}^{′}(1)=4$" :question/worked-solution "If a second-order differential equation for the function $y(x)$ is given with two conditions specified at the *same* location in the domain of $y,$ then this is an **initial value problem**.\n\nLet's go through each equation in turn.\n\n- The first system is not an initial value problem.  It consists of a differential equation together with two conditions at different points in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=-1$ and $x=2$). This is a **boundary value problem.**\n\n- The second system is not an initial value problem. It contains an equation only. No conditions are specified.\n\n- The third system is an initial value problem. The differential equation is together with two conditions at the same location in the domain of $y(x)$ (i.e., at $x=1$)." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-339254/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2d0a7ede-b896-56c6-9b60-a6aec8eff9e8"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339254"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
